#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kspaceduel; is an space arcade game for two players."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each player controls a ship that flies around the sun and tries to shoot at "
"the other ship. You can play &kspaceduel; with another person, against the "
"computer, or you can have the computer control both ships and play each "
"other."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The idea of the game is simple (but addictive). You try to destroy your "
"opponent before he destroys you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "Be careful not to hit the sun."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid "Rules of the Game"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ship Movement"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each player controls one ship."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "The ships can rotate, accelerate, shoot and lay mines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "Energy"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each ship has an amount of energy (refer to the game options for values)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Ships need energy for rotation, acceleration, shooting and laying mines. A "
"ship gets energy from its solar panels. The amount of energy a ship gets "
"depends on the distance from and direction to the sun. A ship gets more "
"energy near the sun and less energy near the border. It gets the full amount "
"of energy if the sun shines directly on the panels and less or even no "
"energy if the sun shines at an angle to the panel or to the side of the "
"panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "If a ship has no energy it cannot navigate or shoot."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hit points"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Collisions with own or other bullets or mines decrease the hit points of a "
"ship. If two ships collide, the weaker ship is destroyed and the hit points "
"of the stronger ship are decreased by the hit points of the weaker ship plus "
"an amount (Crash Damage). A ship is destroyed when it flies into the sun."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bullets and Mines"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "Bullets fly around the sun like a ship."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Mines have an amount of energy to stay at the same position. When the energy "
"is spent, the mine falls into the sun. Mines near the sun need more energy "
"than those which are further away."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mines can be destroyed with bullets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "By default a ship can have 5 bullets and 3 mines on the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Powerups</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "From time to time powerups appear on the play field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are four different powerups:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Mine</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "The maximum number of mines is increased for the player."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "<term>Bullet</term>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid "The maximum number of bullets is increased for the player."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "Energy (yellow sphere)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "The player gets energy."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shield (blue sphere)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "The player gets hit points"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kspaceduel; screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kspaceduel; Main Screen</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kspaceduel; Main Screen</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can see that the central part of the &kspaceduel; screen is the playing "
"area. To the left and the right are the Red Player's and the Blue Player's "
"stats."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The top box on the player stats, represents the <quote>Hit Points</quote> of "
"the craft."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "The middle box on the player stats, represents the battery power."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "The bottom box on the player stats, shows the number of wins."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "The top of the playing area is occupied by the menubar and toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "The bottom of the playing area is the status bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kspaceduel; has many, many options you can adjust to increase the enjoyment "
"of this game."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration is divided into two sections:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "Player Keys"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keys"
msgstr "Claus"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kspaceduel; has a default set of keys to control the game. For a list of "
"default keys see the section entitled <link linkend=\"keys\">Default key "
"bindings</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keys can be configured by:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"Shortcuts...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will bring up a dialog box which lets you configure all hotkeys, "
"including the keys used for steering the space ships, for firing bullets, "
"and for laying mines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can see that each player (Red and Blue), have 5 keystrokes corresponding "
"to Rotate Left, Rotate Right, Accelerate, Shot, and Mines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are finished configuring your keys, you should click on "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton> to apply your changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to restore the default keys, simply click on the "
"<guibutton>Default</guibutton> button once. To make these changes permenant, "
"press <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to abandon the changes you made, and return to your previously "
"selected keys, simply click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton>, and your changes "
"will be lost."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "All game settings of &kspaceduel; are configurable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to change the game settings, simply select "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kspaceduel;..."
"</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will bring up a dialog box with two pages, labelled <guilabel>General</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Game</guilabel>. The first page is rather simple, "
"the second one has seven tabs across the top."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Settings are collected in different configurations. You can choose from "
"several pre-defined configurations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you choose the <guilabel>Custom</guilabel> configuration, you can define "
"all settings for yourself."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have not selected <guilabel>Custom</guilabel>, you will not be able "
"to make any changes to these options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have found an interesting configuration, mail it to the author of the "
"game. It can be implemented in a future version (send the part [Game] in the "
"file <filename>~/.kde/share/config/kspaceduelrc</filename>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you are finished altering the options, you should click on "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton> to apply your changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to restore the default, simply click on the <guibutton>Default</"
"guibutton> button once. To make these changes permenant, press "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want to abandon the changes you made, and return to your previous "
"options, simply click <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton>, and your changes will "
"be lost."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:252
#, no-c-format
msgid "The settings are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
